1
00:00:06,480 --> 00:00:08,000
I thought this project should've been

2
00:00:08,039 --> 00:00:10,320
a perfect wrap-up before you left for America.

3
00:00:10,360 --> 00:00:11,720
Dammit.

4
00:00:11,760 --> 00:00:12,920
We've been played for fools.

5
00:00:12,960 --> 00:00:13,960
You told me

6
00:00:13,960 --> 00:00:15,640
that there was no way you'd ever be into guys.

7
00:00:16,560 --> 00:00:18,120
I admit...

8
00:00:18,160 --> 00:00:19,520
that I act like a tyrant

9
00:00:19,560 --> 00:00:20,520
and have a nasty temper,

10
00:00:20,520 --> 00:00:22,120
but I've never tried to hurt anyone.

11
00:00:22,120 --> 00:00:24,200
You think you can just play me for a fool?

12
00:00:25,120 --> 00:00:26,280
You wanna die that badly?

13
00:00:27,680 --> 00:00:28,800
Okay, maybe a little bit.

14
00:00:30,360 --> 00:00:32,119
Every time I ask you something, you know nothing.

15
00:00:32,119 --> 00:00:33,240
Dammit.

16
00:00:34,040 --> 00:00:35,240
Pite, start talking.

17
00:00:35,280 --> 00:00:36,720
Hey, P'Ing.

18
00:00:38,360 --> 00:00:39,600
I need to have a word with you.

19
00:00:41,240 --> 00:00:42,360
Dammit.

20
00:01:05,319 --> 00:01:06,240
P'Ing.

21
00:01:06,800 --> 00:01:08,240
Eat your food.

22
00:01:09,960 --> 00:01:11,680
You're so sweet. Even blew on it for me?

23
00:01:24,080 --> 00:01:25,240
Hello, Mom.

24
00:02:05,000 --> 00:02:05,840
What's that?

25
00:02:06,880 --> 00:02:07,640
Well,

26
00:02:08,880 --> 00:02:09,720
it's a countdown calendar

27
00:02:09,759 --> 00:02:11,320
until you leave for America.

28
00:02:11,800 --> 00:02:13,920
I want it to be something memorable.

29
00:02:14,880 --> 00:02:16,200
Didn't know you do this stuff, too.

30
00:02:16,240 --> 00:02:17,880
Yeah, don't worry.

31
00:02:18,720 --> 00:02:20,440
I'll keep you busy every single night.

32
00:02:25,320 --> 00:02:25,400
[Secret Recipe for Shrimp Porridge]

33
00:02:59,320 --> 00:03:02,000
P'Ing, what happened to your face?

34
00:03:07,760 --> 00:03:08,560
Look familiar?

35
00:03:11,320 --> 00:03:14,360
The investment firm involved with Green Agriculture.

36
00:03:18,880 --> 00:03:20,160
Are you not saying anything?

37
00:03:25,240 --> 00:03:27,120
It's true I started this company with Itt,

38
00:03:27,120 --> 00:03:27,720
but...

39
00:03:30,720 --> 00:03:31,520
Damn you...

40
00:03:33,400 --> 00:03:35,720
You're a damn good actor.

41
00:03:36,280 --> 00:03:37,360
What did I ever do to you?

42
00:03:38,200 --> 00:03:39,280
You slept with me,

43
00:03:39,320 --> 00:03:40,480
betrayed me,

44
00:03:40,520 --> 00:03:42,600
and gave my stuff to your crush.

45
00:03:44,120 --> 00:03:46,120
P'Ing, it's not like that.

46
00:03:46,160 --> 00:03:47,960
It's true I helped Itt, but...

47
00:03:48,960 --> 00:03:50,480
after that storm,

48
00:03:51,400 --> 00:03:53,120
I told him I was backing out.

49
00:03:53,560 --> 00:03:55,079
I didn't want to hurt you.

50
00:03:56,440 --> 00:03:57,560
You helped him

51
00:03:58,040 --> 00:03:59,320
but didn't want to hurt me?

52
00:04:00,480 --> 00:04:01,720
You sure know...

53
00:04:04,200 --> 00:04:06,320
how to keep the surprises coming.

54
00:04:08,000 --> 00:04:09,000
-Let go. -P'Ing.

55
00:04:09,680 --> 00:04:10,440
Hey.

56
00:04:11,760 --> 00:04:12,920
Please hear me out.

57
00:04:14,600 --> 00:04:16,519
I used to think you were actually an enemy,

58
00:04:17,760 --> 00:04:19,200
but now I know...

59
00:04:19,360 --> 00:04:20,640
that you're not like that.

60
00:04:22,480 --> 00:04:24,080
You were willing to risk your life for me.

61
00:04:24,880 --> 00:04:27,520
I've loved you ever since then.

62
00:04:31,000 --> 00:04:31,800
You've loved me?

63
00:04:39,400 --> 00:04:41,000
Thanks so much

64
00:04:41,720 --> 00:04:44,000
for giving me all the love that wasn't even real.

65
00:04:46,640 --> 00:04:48,040
You've accomplished what you wanted.

66
00:04:49,240 --> 00:04:50,040
Wow,

67
00:04:50,159 --> 00:04:52,159
you even forced yourself to cook for me

68
00:04:52,600 --> 00:04:54,000
and made me think I'd get to top you.

69
00:04:55,240 --> 00:04:56,520
You're just...

70
00:04:57,320 --> 00:04:58,600
an incredible actor.

71
00:04:58,640 --> 00:05:00,040
You deserve an Oscar.

72
00:05:00,960 --> 00:05:01,760
P'Ing.

73
00:05:03,160 --> 00:05:05,240
Please don't treat my feelings like they meant nothing.

74
00:05:06,680 --> 00:05:08,480
What happened between us wasn't a lie.

75
00:05:09,960 --> 00:05:11,840
I can feel that you really love me.

76
00:05:14,160 --> 00:05:14,880
Yeah.

77
00:05:16,360 --> 00:05:17,720
I'll admit it.

78
00:05:17,920 --> 00:05:19,120
I did love you,

79
00:05:21,360 --> 00:05:22,680
but didn't Itt ever tell you?

80
00:05:23,960 --> 00:05:25,720
Plenty of people want me.

81
00:05:26,240 --> 00:05:27,560
It doesn't have to be you.

82
00:05:30,080 --> 00:05:31,440
Listen to me, Yok.

83
00:05:33,360 --> 00:05:34,440
From this moment on,

84
00:05:35,480 --> 00:05:36,760
you and I...

85
00:05:38,880 --> 00:05:40,000
We're over.

86
00:05:40,040 --> 00:05:40,920
No, P'Ing.

87
00:05:40,960 --> 00:05:42,960
Hey, P'Ing.

88
00:05:43,159 --> 00:05:44,000
P'Ing... Hey.

89
00:05:47,280 --> 00:05:48,880
I'm leaving tomorrow.

90
00:05:49,360 --> 00:05:51,159
We can't end things like this.

91
00:05:55,440 --> 00:05:56,360
Let me go.

92
00:05:56,520 --> 00:05:58,320
Didn't you tell me

93
00:05:59,159 --> 00:06:00,600
that this is my home, too?

94
00:06:00,640 --> 00:06:01,440
Shut up.

95
00:06:02,120 --> 00:06:04,120
You have no right to call this place home.

96
00:06:07,640 --> 00:06:09,040
Give me my mom's necklace.

97
00:06:09,480 --> 00:06:10,720
Give me back my mom's necklace.

98
00:06:12,840 --> 00:06:13,600
Dammit.

99
00:06:13,640 --> 00:06:14,720
You piece of...

100
00:06:15,440 --> 00:06:16,240
Damn.

101
00:06:18,000 --> 00:06:19,800
Unbelievably disgusting.

102
00:06:19,800 --> 00:06:21,120
All of you.

103
00:06:22,560 --> 00:06:24,160
All you wanted was to use me.

104
00:06:24,440 --> 00:06:25,320
Screw you.

105
00:06:25,520 --> 00:06:26,360
Can't believe I lowered myself

106
00:06:26,400 --> 00:06:27,600
to your level.

107
00:06:31,440 --> 00:06:32,159
P'Ing...

108
00:06:33,680 --> 00:06:34,880
Don't do this.

109
00:06:44,400 --> 00:06:45,960
If you want to stay, fine.

110
00:06:45,960 --> 00:06:47,840
Whatever it is you want, just take it all.

111
00:06:49,120 --> 00:06:49,960
-P'Ing... -Let me go.

112
00:06:50,000 --> 00:06:51,159
-I said, let me go. -P'Ing.

113
00:06:51,159 --> 00:06:52,480
-Let me go. -P'Ing...

114
00:07:48,960 --> 00:07:52,280
♪ I know my mouth runs hot ♪

115
00:07:52,960 --> 00:07:56,120
♪ I know I bite the hand ♪

116
00:07:56,840 --> 00:08:00,040
♪ I laugh when I should stop ♪

117
00:08:00,840 --> 00:08:03,760
♪ Then I pull you back in ♪

118
00:08:04,520 --> 00:08:07,840
♪ Gold on my bad idea ♪

119
00:10:24,360 --> 00:10:25,520
It's true I helped Itt,

120
00:10:25,560 --> 00:10:25,800
but...

121
00:10:25,840 --> 00:10:26,760
-Please don't treat my feelings -after...

122
00:10:26,800 --> 00:10:27,680
-like they meant nothing. -that storm,

123
00:10:27,720 --> 00:10:28,280
I told him

124
00:10:28,280 --> 00:10:29,160
-I was backing out. -What happened between us

125
00:10:29,160 --> 00:10:30,720
-I didn't want to hurt you. -wasn't a lie.

126
00:10:30,960 --> 00:10:31,840
-I used to think -I'm leaving...

127
00:10:31,880 --> 00:10:32,920
-you were actually an enemy, -tomorrow.

128
00:10:32,920 --> 00:10:34,520
We can't end things like this.

129
00:10:34,520 --> 00:10:36,000
Isn't this my home, too?

130
00:10:36,000 --> 00:10:36,840
Shut up.

131
00:10:40,880 --> 00:10:41,880
Mr. Ing...

132
00:10:44,480 --> 00:10:45,880
Are you awake?

133
00:10:49,400 --> 00:10:50,400
Mr. Ing...

134
00:10:59,840 --> 00:11:00,960
Are you up?

135
00:11:02,120 --> 00:11:03,400
Get a doctor in here.

136
00:11:06,120 --> 00:11:07,680
I don't care if they give me drugs,

137
00:11:07,720 --> 00:11:09,000
an injection, or electric shocks.

138
00:11:09,240 --> 00:11:11,120
Just make it all stop so I can finally rest.

139
00:11:15,440 --> 00:11:18,120
I understand you're too stressed to sleep,

140
00:11:18,160 --> 00:11:19,040
but...

141
00:11:19,080 --> 00:11:20,640
if you just need rest,

142
00:11:20,680 --> 00:11:23,640
that amount of medication might be too much.

143
00:11:25,840 --> 00:11:27,600
The expense paperwork

144
00:11:27,600 --> 00:11:28,520
has all been sorted out,

145
00:11:28,520 --> 00:11:32,120
and I brought some of my husband's clothes for you.

146
00:11:32,520 --> 00:11:35,080
You'll have to make do with these.

147
00:11:37,800 --> 00:11:39,000
I'm sorry

148
00:11:41,000 --> 00:11:43,080
for making you work this late

149
00:11:43,080 --> 00:11:45,240
and having you clean up my messes again.

150
00:11:46,080 --> 00:11:48,640
It's alright. I'm more than happy to help.

151
00:11:50,080 --> 00:11:51,400
You should...

152
00:11:51,440 --> 00:11:53,520
take this opportunity to get plenty of rest.

153
00:12:04,440 --> 00:12:05,440
Wait.

154
00:12:15,600 --> 00:12:16,800
What about that idiot?

155
00:12:20,560 --> 00:12:21,400
Mr. Yok?

156
00:12:21,720 --> 00:12:22,720
Yeah.

157
00:12:22,840 --> 00:12:25,600
He suffered a mild concussion.

158
00:12:26,040 --> 00:12:27,800
He was still unconscious when he arrived,

159
00:12:28,080 --> 00:12:29,720
but the doctor said

160
00:12:29,920 --> 00:12:31,800
there's no internal damage.

161
00:12:32,160 --> 00:12:33,960
He should be waking up soon.

162
00:12:36,240 --> 00:12:38,000
Already did some digging, huh?

163
00:12:39,760 --> 00:12:42,600
Would you like to go see him?

164
00:12:42,600 --> 00:12:43,400
No.

165
00:12:46,760 --> 00:12:47,920
Have you contacted Mr. Phet?

166
00:12:48,640 --> 00:12:51,440
Yes. He should be here any moment.

167
00:12:56,480 --> 00:12:59,520
Are you going somewhere?

168
00:13:04,320 --> 00:13:05,720
Take those clothes back with you.

169
00:13:05,720 --> 00:13:07,000
I have my own.

170
00:13:08,840 --> 00:13:09,680
I see.

171
00:13:10,440 --> 00:13:11,240
Understood.

172
00:13:12,720 --> 00:13:15,160
Take all those gifts, too.

173
00:13:18,560 --> 00:13:20,160
Arrange for my discharge from the hospital.

174
00:13:20,760 --> 00:13:21,720
But the doctor said

175
00:13:21,720 --> 00:13:24,280
you should stay for at least one more night.

176
00:13:24,440 --> 00:13:25,520
Why do I need to stay?

177
00:13:26,160 --> 00:13:27,440
I'm perfectly fine.

178
00:13:41,720 --> 00:13:42,600
Mr. Ing...

179
00:13:47,040 --> 00:13:47,840
Mr. Ing...

180
00:14:06,440 --> 00:14:08,440
Mom, I'm hungry.

181
00:14:08,720 --> 00:14:10,320
I'll find you something to eat, okay?

182
00:14:15,760 --> 00:14:20,480
♪ Buried underneath my smoke-stained cloak ♪

183
00:14:22,200 --> 00:14:27,640
♪ I wore my pride to shield my broken side ♪

184
00:14:27,720 --> 00:14:28,520
Mom...

185
00:14:28,720 --> 00:14:30,200
Please be okay, Mom.

186
00:14:30,480 --> 00:14:31,400
Mom...

187
00:14:33,000 --> 00:14:33,760
Mom.

188
00:14:33,800 --> 00:14:35,400
Relatives aren't allowed inside.

189
00:14:35,760 --> 00:14:36,720
Mom.

190
00:14:37,560 --> 00:14:39,320
Please wait outside.

191
00:14:40,240 --> 00:14:41,280
Mom...

192
00:14:46,520 --> 00:14:47,560
Mom.

193
00:14:50,800 --> 00:14:53,840
♪ I carry thorns inside my chest ♪

194
00:14:54,040 --> 00:14:54,880
Mom...

195
00:14:54,880 --> 00:14:57,280
♪ The pain has never let me rest ♪

196
00:14:57,280 --> 00:15:03,280
♪ If I could turn back the tide once more, ♪

197
00:15:05,000 --> 00:15:10,400
♪ Maybe I could find what I'm looking for ♪

198
00:15:13,240 --> 00:15:18,480
♪ Words unsaid ♪

199
00:15:18,480 --> 00:15:21,080
♪ Silence echoes ♪

200
00:15:22,800 --> 00:15:28,720
♪ In the depths of memories ♪

201
00:15:42,960 --> 00:15:44,560
Thanks so much

202
00:15:45,280 --> 00:15:47,400
for giving me all the love that wasn't even real.

203
00:15:47,400 --> 00:15:48,240
Can't believe I lowered myself

204
00:15:48,280 --> 00:15:49,280
-to your level. -You slept with me,

205
00:15:49,320 --> 00:15:50,080
betrayed me.

206
00:15:50,120 --> 00:15:51,000
Unbelievably disgusting.

207
00:15:51,040 --> 00:15:52,120
And you gave my stuff to your crush.

208
00:15:52,160 --> 00:15:53,240
All of you.

209
00:15:53,280 --> 00:15:54,280
I said, let me go.

210
00:15:54,280 --> 00:15:54,760
Let me...

211
00:16:00,360 --> 00:16:01,080
Yok...

212
00:16:02,000 --> 00:16:02,920
Are you awake?

213
00:16:10,080 --> 00:16:11,040
How are you feeling?

214
00:16:14,040 --> 00:16:15,200
Why are you here?

215
00:16:16,680 --> 00:16:18,160
Mr. Ing's secretary called me.

216
00:16:19,520 --> 00:16:20,960
What happened between you and Mr. Ing?

217
00:16:22,800 --> 00:16:24,400
I can feel that you really love me.

218
00:16:24,480 --> 00:16:25,480
I said, let me go.

219
00:16:27,800 --> 00:16:28,920
Where's P'Ing?

220
00:16:29,520 --> 00:16:30,480
Have you met him yet?

221
00:16:30,720 --> 00:16:31,600
Not yet.

222
00:16:32,200 --> 00:16:33,080
Why do you ask?

223
00:16:34,880 --> 00:16:35,680
Well...

224
00:16:36,800 --> 00:16:38,520
I was hit by a car yesterday.

225
00:16:40,120 --> 00:16:41,640
Please don't tell Mom and Dad yet.

226
00:16:42,520 --> 00:16:43,960
I don't want them to worry.

227
00:16:47,040 --> 00:16:48,840
But Mr. Ing's secretary told me...

228
00:16:49,040 --> 00:16:50,480
that you just fell down.

229
00:16:53,480 --> 00:16:54,160
I did.

230
00:16:55,120 --> 00:16:58,160
I was getting out of the car, but I fell down.

231
00:17:01,120 --> 00:17:02,320
Tell me the truth.

232
00:17:02,920 --> 00:17:04,359
What exactly happened?

233
00:17:06,400 --> 00:17:07,319
P'Phet,

234
00:17:08,160 --> 00:17:09,960
I have my reasons.

235
00:17:10,000 --> 00:17:12,000
Can you not ask me about it right now?

236
00:17:14,640 --> 00:17:16,119
I'll let everything else slide for now,

237
00:17:17,000 --> 00:17:18,480
but I'll need to sort out your problems.

238
00:17:24,240 --> 00:17:25,200
Hello, sir.

239
00:17:25,720 --> 00:17:26,800
Get some rest.

240
00:17:27,200 --> 00:17:28,920
I'll pick you up once you're discharged.

241
00:17:29,720 --> 00:17:30,520
Okay.

242
00:17:49,680 --> 00:17:50,640
Take good care of him.

243
00:17:50,800 --> 00:17:51,680
Yes, sir.

244
00:18:19,120 --> 00:18:20,440
[Calling P'Ing]

245
00:18:30,280 --> 00:18:32,760
[P'Ing]

246
00:18:32,800 --> 00:18:34,800
[Block Caller]

247
00:18:34,840 --> 00:18:35,160
[Yok]

248
00:18:35,200 --> 00:18:36,160
[Yok: Blocked]

249
00:18:37,200 --> 00:18:38,840
You don't know when to quit, do you?

250
00:18:50,240 --> 00:18:51,880
Oh, Mr. Ing?

251
00:18:52,640 --> 00:18:54,800
What brings you here so suddenly?

252
00:18:56,960 --> 00:18:57,880
Please come in.

253
00:19:04,320 --> 00:19:06,320
If I'd known you were coming,

254
00:19:06,840 --> 00:19:08,760
I would've made sure the place was spotless.

255
00:19:10,080 --> 00:19:12,280
Yeah, it's fine.

256
00:19:13,200 --> 00:19:14,320
I don't mind.

257
00:19:16,720 --> 00:19:19,000
You're staying here tonight?

258
00:19:20,440 --> 00:19:21,160
Yeah.

259
00:19:21,880 --> 00:19:24,080
Let me put your suitcase away.

260
00:19:25,960 --> 00:19:26,960
This way, please.

261
00:19:47,320 --> 00:19:49,440
Are you still working at Vince's barber shop?

262
00:19:50,080 --> 00:19:51,920
He said that I'm slow

263
00:19:52,560 --> 00:19:53,880
and not very sharp,

264
00:19:54,920 --> 00:19:57,440
so he suggested I learn hairdressing somewhere else.

265
00:19:57,600 --> 00:19:58,440
That's for the best.

266
00:19:58,920 --> 00:20:01,320
You shouldn't be hanging around him anyway.

267
00:20:03,240 --> 00:20:04,520
Would you like to sit down first

268
00:20:04,720 --> 00:20:06,880
to see if it's too soft or too hard?

269
00:20:09,320 --> 00:20:10,400
It's okay.

270
00:20:11,720 --> 00:20:12,800
I can sleep on pretty much anything.

271
00:20:28,920 --> 00:20:31,040
I'll let them keep you company tonight.

272
00:20:39,880 --> 00:20:40,800
What?

273
00:20:40,800 --> 00:20:41,560
Do you like it?

274
00:20:41,600 --> 00:20:43,280
I'll buy a couple for you.

275
00:20:43,520 --> 00:20:45,160
-No, thanks. -What?

276
00:20:45,400 --> 00:20:46,240
Why not?

277
00:20:46,360 --> 00:20:48,240
I thought kids these days were into this stuff.

278
00:20:48,880 --> 00:20:50,920
Trends come and go every other day.

279
00:20:51,160 --> 00:20:52,240
It's nonsense.

280
00:20:54,120 --> 00:20:55,240
So you're saying...

281
00:20:55,800 --> 00:20:58,000
that you're too cool for this?

282
00:20:58,040 --> 00:20:59,920
If you're old-fashioned, just admit it.

283
00:20:59,960 --> 00:21:01,400
Like, those who can't keep up with the trends.

284
00:21:01,880 --> 00:21:04,160
I call my style classic.

285
00:21:05,040 --> 00:21:06,840
"I call my style classic."

286
00:21:06,880 --> 00:21:08,480
Why are you trying so hard to look cool?

287
00:21:10,960 --> 00:21:11,920
Put them away.

288
00:21:13,280 --> 00:21:14,880
I'm not really fond of these things.

289
00:21:17,280 --> 00:21:18,080
Okay.

290
00:21:25,960 --> 00:21:27,520
Well, good night.

291
00:22:04,600 --> 00:22:06,640
Young Master, you have a visitor.

292
00:22:26,280 --> 00:22:28,680
After everything you've done to get this chance,

293
00:22:29,160 --> 00:22:30,440
you're throwing it away now?

294
00:22:35,080 --> 00:22:36,200
It's my fault.

295
00:22:37,360 --> 00:22:39,560
I'll pay the contract termination fee myself.

296
00:22:39,560 --> 00:22:41,320
It's not about the money.

297
00:22:43,840 --> 00:22:45,240
What made you change your mind?

298
00:22:47,320 --> 00:22:49,200
I've lost someone...

299
00:22:50,200 --> 00:22:51,600
I never should've let go.

300
00:22:55,720 --> 00:22:57,400
Just because of love?

301
00:22:58,520 --> 00:22:59,760
It made you throw away the chance

302
00:22:59,800 --> 00:23:02,360
to be in the world-class boxing ring?

303
00:23:08,560 --> 00:23:09,680
P'Khun,

304
00:23:10,920 --> 00:23:12,240
I've really thought this through

305
00:23:12,880 --> 00:23:14,280
and decided to quit professional boxing.

306
00:23:15,920 --> 00:23:17,080
I used to think...

307
00:23:17,720 --> 00:23:19,640
that being in the ring

308
00:23:21,160 --> 00:23:23,120
was the only time I could be myself,

309
00:23:28,040 --> 00:23:30,360
but then someone made me feel the same way.

310
00:23:30,840 --> 00:23:32,080
How were you raised?

311
00:23:32,200 --> 00:23:34,000
We're humans. Just do whatever you want.

312
00:23:34,240 --> 00:23:35,440
Eat whatever you want.

313
00:23:35,680 --> 00:23:37,280
Why overthink everything?

314
00:23:37,800 --> 00:23:38,880
-Twist upward. -Like this?

315
00:23:38,880 --> 00:23:39,880
-Twist. -Twist upward?

316
00:23:40,440 --> 00:23:41,000
Like this?

317
00:23:41,040 --> 00:23:42,040
P'Ing.

318
00:23:42,040 --> 00:23:42,960
Do you actually want to learn?

319
00:23:47,280 --> 00:23:48,280
P'Ing.

320
00:23:48,280 --> 00:23:50,280
If you ever need to let it all out,

321
00:23:51,920 --> 00:23:52,960
I'm right here for you.

322
00:23:53,920 --> 00:23:55,000
Let me give you a reward.

323
00:23:56,800 --> 00:23:58,480
Your heart belongs to me.

324
00:23:58,840 --> 00:24:01,160
No matter where in the world you go,

325
00:24:01,400 --> 00:24:03,040
you'll still be thinking of me.

326
00:24:07,000 --> 00:24:08,920
Maybe I never wanted to be a pro boxer.

327
00:24:11,320 --> 00:24:13,200
I'm sorry for letting you down.

328
00:24:31,880 --> 00:24:34,080
That was for the talent you're throwing away

329
00:24:34,560 --> 00:24:36,720
and the concern I wasted on you.

330
00:24:44,560 --> 00:24:45,720
As for the fee,

331
00:24:46,600 --> 00:24:47,760
I'll take care of it.

332
00:24:49,160 --> 00:24:49,920
At most, I'll just say,

333
00:24:49,960 --> 00:24:51,280
"This kid's lost his mind,

334
00:24:52,280 --> 00:24:53,600
and it's better that he's out of the gym."

335
00:25:00,480 --> 00:25:02,360
Just be a sparring partner for me sometimes.

336
00:25:03,680 --> 00:25:04,960
None of these new kids

337
00:25:06,400 --> 00:25:08,600
can match your stamina.

338
00:25:11,960 --> 00:25:12,760
I will.

339
00:25:14,520 --> 00:25:16,360
Thank you, P'Khun.

340
00:26:00,320 --> 00:26:00,960
[Itt: P'Ing.]

341
00:26:00,960 --> 00:26:02,720
[If you're going to blame someone, blame me.]

342
00:26:02,720 --> 00:26:03,920
[Don't blame Yok.]

343
00:26:11,000 --> 00:26:11,920
Mr. Ing.

344
00:26:12,360 --> 00:26:13,440
Mr. Muangthep just called.

345
00:26:13,440 --> 00:26:15,320
He's found someone who can stop

346
00:26:15,320 --> 00:26:16,800
the Pattaya project from getting approved.

347
00:26:17,480 --> 00:26:18,400
But...

348
00:26:18,440 --> 00:26:21,560
shall we proceed with it?

349
00:26:27,400 --> 00:26:29,080
Tell him...

350
00:26:31,080 --> 00:26:32,440
that if he pulls this off,

351
00:26:33,920 --> 00:26:36,120
he'll get everything he wants from me.

352
00:26:38,400 --> 00:26:39,920
But if the project gets suspended,

353
00:26:41,200 --> 00:26:42,720
you, Mr. Itt, and Mr. Yok will...

354
00:26:42,720 --> 00:26:43,760
Secretary Piang,

355
00:26:44,120 --> 00:26:46,400
I've spent the last two days thinking it over.

356
00:26:46,720 --> 00:26:49,400
Stealing our condo units

357
00:26:49,440 --> 00:26:51,640
and reaching out to that couple

358
00:26:53,880 --> 00:26:55,760
must've taken a lot of planning.

359
00:26:57,080 --> 00:27:00,240
If I let those brats get away with this,

360
00:27:01,680 --> 00:27:02,520
don't you call me

361
00:27:02,560 --> 00:27:03,920
Ing of Araya Group.

362
00:27:05,640 --> 00:27:06,720
After this,

363
00:27:06,920 --> 00:27:08,440
they're going to lose that land

364
00:27:08,440 --> 00:27:09,800
they practically got for free.

365
00:27:12,320 --> 00:27:13,120
Green Agriculture

366
00:27:13,160 --> 00:27:15,040
and those brats' firm

367
00:27:15,920 --> 00:27:17,960
are in for some serious damage.

368
00:27:19,800 --> 00:27:21,800
Whether they can find the cash flow

369
00:27:23,720 --> 00:27:25,480
or pull their shares out in time,

370
00:27:26,800 --> 00:27:27,800
in the end,

371
00:27:29,120 --> 00:27:30,920
they're screwed either way.

372
00:27:32,480 --> 00:27:34,040
But they're just getting started.

373
00:27:34,080 --> 00:27:36,080
If we cut off their investment funds,

374
00:27:36,120 --> 00:27:37,600
they won't give up that easily.

375
00:27:38,080 --> 00:27:39,840
They'll keep dragging it out,

376
00:27:39,880 --> 00:27:41,000
refusing to let it end.

377
00:27:43,560 --> 00:27:44,520
Secretary Piang,

378
00:27:46,320 --> 00:27:47,520
you have the wrong idea.

379
00:27:48,320 --> 00:27:49,640
I'm not trying to drag this out.

380
00:27:50,520 --> 00:27:52,440
I want them destroyed.

381
00:27:53,640 --> 00:27:54,800
And I'll be waiting

382
00:27:54,800 --> 00:27:57,080
for the final act of this play

383
00:27:58,120 --> 00:28:00,040
and watching them come up empty-handed.

384
00:28:00,720 --> 00:28:01,760
Eventually,

385
00:28:02,120 --> 00:28:04,720
they'll end up suing each other, right?

386
00:28:07,680 --> 00:28:09,320
It's going to be entertaining as hell.

387
00:28:45,480 --> 00:28:45,720
[P'Ing.]

388
00:28:45,720 --> 00:28:46,160
[Can you please answer me?]

389
00:28:46,200 --> 00:28:46,600
[How are you feeling?]

390
00:28:46,640 --> 00:28:47,040
[Have you eaten?]

391
00:28:47,080 --> 00:28:47,520
[P'Ing, where are you?]

392
00:28:47,560 --> 00:28:48,000
[Are you really not gonna reply?]

393
00:28:48,000 --> 00:28:48,520
[Are you at the office?]

394
00:28:48,520 --> 00:28:49,120
[I'm about to be discharged from the hospital.]

395
00:28:49,160 --> 00:28:49,920
Mr. Yok,

396
00:28:49,960 --> 00:28:51,520
I've finalized

397
00:28:51,560 --> 00:28:52,440
your discharge papers.

398
00:28:52,440 --> 00:28:53,640
Shall we leave now?

399
00:28:53,680 --> 00:28:54,560
Where's P'Phet?

400
00:28:56,040 --> 00:28:56,920
I'm afraid I don't know.

401
00:29:00,400 --> 00:29:01,880
Thank you for the information.

402
00:29:02,560 --> 00:29:03,520
If you'll excuse me.

403
00:29:05,680 --> 00:29:08,040
Dad, what happened to P'Phet?

404
00:29:08,040 --> 00:29:09,320
Still have the nerve to ask me that?

405
00:29:09,360 --> 00:29:11,080
This is all because of the mess you made.

406
00:29:14,160 --> 00:29:16,240
Quit Araya Group right now

407
00:29:16,280 --> 00:29:18,080
and stop seeing Ing once and for all.

408
00:29:18,800 --> 00:29:19,600
Yok,

409
00:29:20,000 --> 00:29:20,600
your brother

410
00:29:20,640 --> 00:29:22,680
has been taken in by the Crime Suppression Division

411
00:29:22,680 --> 00:29:24,080
for questioning.

412
00:29:24,560 --> 00:29:25,320
They found evidence that

413
00:29:25,320 --> 00:29:27,240
Phet was involved in corruption with the Pattaya project.

414
00:29:29,040 --> 00:29:30,160
That's impossible.

415
00:29:30,520 --> 00:29:32,200
He would never do anything like that.

416
00:29:34,800 --> 00:29:36,240
What does P'Ing have to do with this?

417
00:29:36,280 --> 00:29:37,680
It's plain as day.

418
00:29:37,840 --> 00:29:39,480
As soon as his project was taken away,

419
00:29:39,520 --> 00:29:40,920
your brother immediately ran into trouble.

420
00:29:41,320 --> 00:29:43,640
This is clearly an act of revenge.

421
00:29:44,080 --> 00:29:46,520
P'Ing would never play dirty like that.

422
00:29:47,160 --> 00:29:48,360
There must be some mistake.

423
00:29:48,400 --> 00:29:50,080
You're still calling him P'Ing?

424
00:29:50,320 --> 00:29:52,400
With a situation like this,

425
00:29:53,160 --> 00:29:54,560
if we can't find evidence

426
00:29:54,560 --> 00:29:56,280
to prove your brother's innocence,

427
00:29:56,600 --> 00:29:58,680
his future is completely over.

428
00:30:00,120 --> 00:30:01,720
His entire life,

429
00:30:01,840 --> 00:30:04,240
he's never caused me any trouble.

430
00:30:04,440 --> 00:30:05,560
But then you started working

431
00:30:05,560 --> 00:30:07,200
for those people at Araya Group.

432
00:30:07,240 --> 00:30:08,640
That's why this happened.

433
00:30:09,120 --> 00:30:11,120
I shouldn't have let you work for them.

434
00:30:14,960 --> 00:30:16,120
I'll find out

435
00:30:16,240 --> 00:30:17,680
who's really behind this.

436
00:30:21,600 --> 00:30:23,040
I need to take this call.

437
00:30:23,040 --> 00:30:23,960
Wait.

438
00:30:26,520 --> 00:30:27,520
Look at him.

439
00:30:29,280 --> 00:30:30,880
What should we do?

440
00:30:33,680 --> 00:30:35,760
[Incoming Call: Itt]

441
00:30:38,240 --> 00:30:38,920
Yok.

442
00:30:39,120 --> 00:30:41,520
My brother has found someone to stop the Pattaya project.

443
00:30:41,640 --> 00:30:42,920
He's not going to give up.

444
00:30:43,320 --> 00:30:44,760
I have nothing to do with your plans.

445
00:30:45,000 --> 00:30:46,120
You don't need to tell me anything.

446
00:30:46,280 --> 00:30:48,080
I just want you to be careful.

447
00:30:48,200 --> 00:30:50,000
I heard P'Phet would be taken in for questioning.

448
00:30:50,440 --> 00:30:52,120
It must be P'Ing's doing.

449
00:30:53,240 --> 00:30:55,400
You know how vengeful he is.

450
00:30:55,920 --> 00:30:56,640
Yok,

451
00:30:57,920 --> 00:30:59,520
you should work with me again.

452
00:31:05,800 --> 00:31:07,120
It's not P'Ing's doing.

453
00:31:07,120 --> 00:31:09,040
Still making excuses for him?

454
00:31:09,720 --> 00:31:10,600
Do you like him so much

455
00:31:10,640 --> 00:31:12,120
that you'd actually let P'Phet go to jail?

456
00:31:17,200 --> 00:31:18,080
Dad...

457
00:31:18,080 --> 00:31:19,240
I'm heading out.

458
00:31:19,280 --> 00:31:20,320
Give me a moment.

459
00:31:21,280 --> 00:31:22,680
-Look at him. -Yok...

460
00:31:23,120 --> 00:31:24,400
Where are you going?

461
00:31:25,160 --> 00:31:26,400
We haven't finished talking yet.

462
00:31:31,960 --> 00:31:33,440
[System: No SIM]

463
00:31:42,720 --> 00:31:44,600
Hello?

464
00:31:46,080 --> 00:31:46,920
Who is this?

465
00:31:47,520 --> 00:31:49,520
Oh? And who are you?

466
00:31:49,560 --> 00:31:52,160
The owner of this phone wanted me to ask that question.

467
00:31:53,440 --> 00:31:54,760
Put P'Ing on the phone.

468
00:31:55,280 --> 00:31:57,240
Mr. Ing, you have a call.

469
00:32:01,520 --> 00:32:02,320
Hello?

470
00:32:03,080 --> 00:32:04,600
It's me. Where are you?

471
00:32:10,080 --> 00:32:11,680
I think he's your type.

472
00:32:12,160 --> 00:32:14,400
If you want him, tell him where we are.

473
00:32:15,800 --> 00:32:17,160
Hi, handsome.

474
00:32:17,680 --> 00:32:20,320
We're at SB Bar.

475
00:32:25,040 --> 00:32:28,120
Oh? Why'd he hang up so fast?

476
00:32:28,600 --> 00:32:30,080
He probably...

477
00:32:30,680 --> 00:32:32,680
can't wait to see us.

478
00:32:52,680 --> 00:32:54,680
Wow, we got someone.

479
00:33:02,520 --> 00:33:03,520
-Do you know who he is? -Go ahead.

480
00:33:03,520 --> 00:33:04,160
-Who are you? -You can order

481
00:33:04,200 --> 00:33:05,120
whatever you want.

482
00:33:05,320 --> 00:33:06,920
Don't worry about the money.

483
00:33:08,080 --> 00:33:09,400
I said don't worry.

484
00:33:20,160 --> 00:33:20,960
P'Ing?

485
00:33:21,680 --> 00:33:23,440
Who is this?

486
00:33:24,360 --> 00:33:25,480
Oh...

487
00:33:26,360 --> 00:33:27,320
He's the youngest son

488
00:33:27,320 --> 00:33:29,440
of Minister Pongpaisan.

489
00:33:30,400 --> 00:33:31,600
Is that so?

490
00:33:33,400 --> 00:33:35,000
Tell me.

491
00:33:35,720 --> 00:33:37,240
Between me and him,

492
00:33:37,920 --> 00:33:39,200
who's hotter?

493
00:33:43,200 --> 00:33:44,480
It has to be you, Mr. Ing.

494
00:33:46,200 --> 00:33:47,000
P'Ing.

495
00:33:49,800 --> 00:33:51,600
I need to talk to you in private.

496
00:33:54,440 --> 00:33:55,520
Hey.

497
00:33:56,280 --> 00:33:58,440
Take Mr. Muangthep to the room next door

498
00:33:58,840 --> 00:34:00,360
and get him a bottle of Royal Salute.

499
00:34:00,680 --> 00:34:01,760
Put it on my tab.

500
00:34:02,600 --> 00:34:03,800
Thank you very much.

501
00:34:04,920 --> 00:34:05,680
Thank you.

502
00:34:06,080 --> 00:34:07,360
Keep me steady, alright?

503
00:34:08,000 --> 00:34:09,080
Then...

504
00:34:09,440 --> 00:34:10,520
I'm leaving.

505
00:34:10,560 --> 00:34:11,440
Wait.

506
00:34:12,520 --> 00:34:13,920
What's there to be afraid of?

507
00:34:14,639 --> 00:34:15,719
You're with me.

508
00:34:22,239 --> 00:34:23,520
Get the hell out!

509
00:34:25,679 --> 00:34:26,760
Please excuse me.

510
00:34:41,560 --> 00:34:44,760
What brings the honorable Minister Pongpaisan's son

511
00:34:46,040 --> 00:34:47,920
to a place like this?

512
00:34:49,600 --> 00:34:50,360
Want some?

513
00:35:03,520 --> 00:35:05,160
Shouldn't you be boxing

514
00:35:05,200 --> 00:35:06,880
in America right now?

515
00:35:07,040 --> 00:35:08,760
What happened? Isn't that your dream?

516
00:35:10,760 --> 00:35:12,480
Or was all that talk...

517
00:35:13,040 --> 00:35:15,040
about wanting to be a boxer

518
00:35:16,080 --> 00:35:18,480
just more of your lies?

519
00:35:19,280 --> 00:35:20,080
Tell me.

520
00:35:21,520 --> 00:35:22,560
I'm so confused right now,

521
00:35:22,600 --> 00:35:23,240
P'Ing.

522
00:35:24,720 --> 00:35:26,320
Was Phet called in for questioning

523
00:35:26,640 --> 00:35:27,960
because of you?

524
00:35:30,120 --> 00:35:32,120
So you only came because of this?

525
00:35:35,040 --> 00:35:36,960
I just wanted to know the truth.

526
00:35:41,360 --> 00:35:42,360
Jeez.

527
00:35:43,640 --> 00:35:45,400
You want the truth? Fine, I'll give it to you.

528
00:35:45,440 --> 00:35:47,240
I stopped the Pattaya project,

529
00:35:47,280 --> 00:35:48,360
and as for your brother,

530
00:35:48,360 --> 00:35:50,800
I called the police on him. Happy now?

531
00:35:56,040 --> 00:35:57,360
Is it true?

532
00:35:59,520 --> 00:36:00,320
Why?

533
00:36:03,800 --> 00:36:05,840
Do you think the great Young Master Yok...

534
00:36:07,160 --> 00:36:08,640
would make mistakes?

535
00:36:09,360 --> 00:36:10,160
Huh?

536
00:36:10,880 --> 00:36:13,120
You know exactly what kind of person I am, don't you?

537
00:36:21,600 --> 00:36:23,600
Instead of wasting your time on me,

538
00:36:24,360 --> 00:36:26,360
you should be helping your brother.

539
00:36:27,560 --> 00:36:28,480
Otherwise,

540
00:36:29,520 --> 00:36:32,120
his future is going to be ruined by my hand.

541
00:36:34,800 --> 00:36:35,640
Got it?

542
00:36:40,200 --> 00:36:41,800
If you're looking for revenge, take it out on me.

543
00:36:41,840 --> 00:36:43,520
Why drag P'Phet into this?

544
00:36:43,960 --> 00:36:45,360
You're saying he knew nothing, huh?

545
00:36:45,640 --> 00:36:47,120
That brother of yours...

546
00:36:47,400 --> 00:36:48,440
If it weren't for him,

547
00:36:48,440 --> 00:36:49,680
how could someone like you

548
00:36:49,720 --> 00:36:50,880
possibly stab me in the back?

549
00:36:50,920 --> 00:36:51,880
Seriously?

550
00:36:57,560 --> 00:36:58,880
He didn't do anything.

551
00:37:02,360 --> 00:37:03,480
Are you mad at me?

552
00:37:04,120 --> 00:37:05,000
Go ahead.

553
00:37:06,200 --> 00:37:07,080
Punch me.

554
00:37:08,040 --> 00:37:08,960
Hit me.

555
00:37:10,400 --> 00:37:12,400
Aren't you a boxer?

556
00:37:13,200 --> 00:37:14,000
Come on.

557
00:37:15,120 --> 00:37:15,920
Punch me.

558
00:37:17,800 --> 00:37:18,680
Let me tell you...

559
00:37:20,880 --> 00:37:21,680
P'Ing,

560
00:37:22,200 --> 00:37:23,120
please stop.

561
00:37:34,640 --> 00:37:35,840
It's your mom.

562
00:37:36,800 --> 00:37:38,200
She seems pretty desperate.

563
00:37:40,000 --> 00:37:41,200
Aren't you going to pick up?

564
00:37:45,520 --> 00:37:46,280
Yok,

565
00:37:46,520 --> 00:37:48,240
come home now.

566
00:37:48,440 --> 00:37:50,560
Dad's found someone who can help.

567
00:37:50,800 --> 00:37:52,680
You have to go there with us right now.

568
00:37:54,560 --> 00:37:55,360
Yes, Mom.

569
00:37:59,960 --> 00:38:01,360
Let me tell you something.

570
00:38:03,480 --> 00:38:04,280
This...

571
00:38:04,680 --> 00:38:05,800
is just the appetizer.

572
00:38:06,560 --> 00:38:07,720
We're not over yet.

573
00:38:07,960 --> 00:38:09,360
You cannot date anyone else.

574
00:38:10,320 --> 00:38:11,880
I'll be keeping an eye on you.

575
00:38:21,600 --> 00:38:25,440
P'Ing, if you want to take your revenge on me, do it.

576
00:38:26,440 --> 00:38:27,480
But please,

577
00:38:28,120 --> 00:38:29,520
don't ruin my brother.

578
00:38:30,560 --> 00:38:31,880
Once this is settled,

579
00:38:32,440 --> 00:38:33,720
I'll come back to you.

580
00:38:33,760 --> 00:38:34,760
When that time comes,

581
00:38:35,560 --> 00:38:36,960
you can do whatever you want

582
00:38:37,520 --> 00:38:38,480
to me.

583
00:38:39,160 --> 00:38:40,160
Who said you could leave?

584
00:38:42,120 --> 00:38:43,360
Things between us aren't over.

585
00:38:43,520 --> 00:38:45,040
You're not leaving me.

586
00:38:54,360 --> 00:38:55,400
Dammit.

587
00:38:56,560 --> 00:38:57,440
Pite,

588
00:38:58,160 --> 00:38:58,880
Itt,

589
00:38:59,560 --> 00:39:00,480
Yok...

590
00:39:01,880 --> 00:39:03,960
Not one of you knows how to be grateful.

591
00:39:13,320 --> 00:39:14,720
I'd really appreciate your help

592
00:39:14,920 --> 00:39:16,320
with Phet's case.

593
00:39:27,720 --> 00:39:29,000
How did it go?

594
00:39:29,040 --> 00:39:30,840
Can they help us at all?

595
00:39:30,920 --> 00:39:32,360
They said that

596
00:39:33,280 --> 00:39:34,760
the whistleblower information

597
00:39:34,800 --> 00:39:37,440
and the source of the evidence are currently sealed.

598
00:39:38,600 --> 00:39:40,640
Even though they trust Phet,

599
00:39:41,080 --> 00:39:42,760
they can't step in to help.

600
00:39:43,920 --> 00:39:45,360
It looks like

601
00:39:46,080 --> 00:39:48,000
this is going to be more complicated than we thought.

602
00:39:55,360 --> 00:39:56,360
Dad,

603
00:39:56,640 --> 00:39:58,160
if he was really framed,

604
00:39:58,160 --> 00:39:58,960
is it possible that

605
00:39:58,960 --> 00:40:00,840
someone secretly opened an account under his name

606
00:40:01,160 --> 00:40:03,240
and transferred that dirty money into it?

607
00:40:04,840 --> 00:40:07,240
In that case, we need to check offshore accounts as well.

608
00:40:09,800 --> 00:40:11,880
I think we need a more specialized approach.

609
00:40:13,200 --> 00:40:14,720
Mom, your brother, Uncle Phao,

610
00:40:14,760 --> 00:40:15,800
has a son named Phu

611
00:40:16,200 --> 00:40:17,800
who graduated with a cybersecurity degree.

612
00:40:21,720 --> 00:40:23,040
Then talk to him immediately.

613
00:40:24,960 --> 00:40:25,920
Drive.

614
00:40:37,880 --> 00:40:39,160
He didn't do anything.

615
00:40:39,520 --> 00:40:40,920
Don't ruin my brother.

616
00:40:41,520 --> 00:40:43,280
Why drag P'Phet into this?

617
00:40:44,440 --> 00:40:45,440
Hey, Ju.

618
00:40:48,320 --> 00:40:49,000
Yes?

619
00:40:50,120 --> 00:40:50,920
Come here.

620
00:41:03,480 --> 00:41:04,880
In your eyes,

621
00:41:06,840 --> 00:41:08,640
am I a good person or a bad one?

622
00:41:13,000 --> 00:41:13,920
I think...

623
00:41:14,720 --> 00:41:16,160
you're a good person

624
00:41:16,600 --> 00:41:18,320
who's just intentionally acting mean.

625
00:41:24,680 --> 00:41:25,480
Why is that?

626
00:41:27,160 --> 00:41:29,680
I think whether someone is good or bad

627
00:41:30,000 --> 00:41:31,480
isn't determined by their words,

628
00:41:32,760 --> 00:41:34,440
but by their actions.

629
00:41:38,640 --> 00:41:41,840
Last time, I was so clumsy

630
00:41:42,840 --> 00:41:44,440
and made a mess of your hair,

631
00:41:46,120 --> 00:41:47,640
but you still gave me a tip.

632
00:41:51,400 --> 00:41:52,600
You're kind.

633
00:42:01,200 --> 00:42:02,200
Look at you.

634
00:42:05,160 --> 00:42:06,880
You're so naive.

635
00:42:16,080 --> 00:42:17,160
Hold on.

636
00:42:18,080 --> 00:42:18,800
What?

637
00:42:19,080 --> 00:42:20,080
Close your eyes.

638
00:42:20,560 --> 00:42:22,480
There's a stray hair on your eyelid.

639
00:42:59,800 --> 00:43:01,120
I'm going for a smoke.

640
00:43:47,760 --> 00:43:49,320
-Good morning. -Hello, sir.

641
00:43:49,360 --> 00:43:51,760
The new runway collection suits you perfectly.

642
00:43:52,080 --> 00:43:53,160
You have good taste.

643
00:43:55,000 --> 00:43:57,400
Ms. Koi and Mr. Third reached out early this morning.

644
00:43:57,720 --> 00:43:59,960
It seems they want to turn over a new leaf,

645
00:43:59,960 --> 00:44:01,480
just as you predicted.

646
00:44:01,960 --> 00:44:03,160
Just leave them hanging.

647
00:44:03,640 --> 00:44:04,640
Don't bother getting back to them.

648
00:44:05,160 --> 00:44:06,560
Let them squirm.

649
00:44:12,440 --> 00:44:14,840
I'm going to sue Yok and Itt's company

650
00:44:15,280 --> 00:44:17,400
for theft of trade secrets.

651
00:44:17,960 --> 00:44:19,200
Get the legal team on this.

652
00:44:19,240 --> 00:44:20,400
It's time they learned

653
00:44:21,040 --> 00:44:22,440
what happens

654
00:44:22,440 --> 00:44:23,440
when they mess with what's mine.

655
00:44:24,120 --> 00:44:25,040
Understood.

656
00:44:26,080 --> 00:44:27,400
Have you contacted Mr. Phet yet?

657
00:44:27,800 --> 00:44:28,640
Yes.

658
00:44:28,640 --> 00:44:29,800
I've scheduled the appointment

659
00:44:29,840 --> 00:44:32,080
for the day after the board meeting.

660
00:44:32,120 --> 00:44:33,000
Good. That way,

661
00:44:33,840 --> 00:44:35,840
we can get everything settled before the end of the year

662
00:44:35,840 --> 00:44:37,040
and make a clean break.

663
00:44:37,680 --> 00:44:38,400
Alright.

664
00:44:38,720 --> 00:44:39,840
This afternoon, summarize and review

665
00:44:40,120 --> 00:44:42,320
the board meeting agenda

666
00:44:42,440 --> 00:44:43,320
because...

667
00:44:43,640 --> 00:44:45,960
my relatives are extremely anxious.

668
00:44:46,280 --> 00:44:47,880
I need to appease them.

669
00:44:49,040 --> 00:44:50,400
My dear old dad

670
00:44:50,440 --> 00:44:52,400
told everyone about that mess in Pattaya.

671
00:44:53,000 --> 00:44:54,080
Now everyone's in a tizzy.

672
00:44:55,000 --> 00:44:56,600
Understood. I'll take care of it.

673
00:44:56,680 --> 00:44:57,360
Yeah.

674
00:44:58,360 --> 00:44:59,160
Please excuse me.

675
00:45:02,800 --> 00:45:03,680
Phet...

676
00:45:04,880 --> 00:45:06,320
Are you okay?

677
00:45:10,360 --> 00:45:12,640
Someone used your name to open an offshore account.

678
00:45:14,000 --> 00:45:15,000
A very sophisticated plan.

679
00:45:15,840 --> 00:45:18,160
P'Phu and I have spent the last two days

680
00:45:18,160 --> 00:45:19,440
tracing the money trail

681
00:45:19,480 --> 00:45:20,400
through seven offshore accounts.

682
00:45:20,800 --> 00:45:22,520
All the transfers came from a virtual account,

683
00:45:23,440 --> 00:45:25,640
but the login IP is fully encrypted.

684
00:45:26,040 --> 00:45:27,040
We need to find the IP address

685
00:45:27,080 --> 00:45:28,920
and identify the person behind the account

686
00:45:29,040 --> 00:45:30,480
before we can dig any deeper.

687
00:45:31,680 --> 00:45:33,360
As for the whistleblower,

688
00:45:33,600 --> 00:45:35,480
P'Phu has managed to hack into the external system.

689
00:45:35,520 --> 00:45:37,000
He's currently checking the call logs.

690
00:45:40,560 --> 00:45:44,800
[P'Phu]

691
00:45:44,920 --> 00:45:46,000
I only found some of it.

692
00:45:46,280 --> 00:45:48,240
Before P'Phet was taken in for questioning,

693
00:45:48,520 --> 00:45:50,680
there was only one person besides the DSI officers

694
00:45:50,840 --> 00:45:52,720
who had ties to the Pattaya project,

695
00:45:52,760 --> 00:45:53,760
and that was...

696
00:45:53,960 --> 00:45:55,960
the secretary of Araya Group's CEO.

697
00:45:58,480 --> 00:46:00,280
Can you find out what they talked about?

698
00:46:00,480 --> 00:46:02,040
They were in contact twice.

699
00:46:02,360 --> 00:46:03,200
The first time,

700
00:46:03,640 --> 00:46:04,560
the office said

701
00:46:04,600 --> 00:46:05,960
they had received the documents she sent

702
00:46:05,960 --> 00:46:07,600
and thanked her for the cooperation.

703
00:46:07,600 --> 00:46:08,720
As for the second time,

704
00:46:08,800 --> 00:46:10,800
it was to schedule their next meeting

705
00:46:11,080 --> 00:46:12,600
to ask for more information.

706
00:46:14,160 --> 00:46:15,280
When is the meeting scheduled for?

707
00:46:15,560 --> 00:46:16,560
The day after tomorrow.

708
00:46:19,880 --> 00:46:20,640
Got it.

709
00:46:22,360 --> 00:46:23,640
Thanks a lot, Phu.

710
00:46:25,040 --> 00:46:25,960
My pleasure.

711
00:46:27,720 --> 00:46:28,600
Yok,

712
00:46:30,160 --> 00:46:31,680
call Ing right now

713
00:46:31,840 --> 00:46:34,440
and ask him exactly what he wants.

714
00:46:34,760 --> 00:46:36,280
Tell him to be straight with us

715
00:46:36,560 --> 00:46:38,200
instead of playing games behind our backs.

716
00:46:41,640 --> 00:46:42,440
Dad,

717
00:46:43,360 --> 00:46:44,320
contacting him privately

718
00:46:44,360 --> 00:46:45,640
could lead to a misunderstanding.

719
00:46:46,080 --> 00:46:47,160
Let's take it easy for now.

720
00:46:49,480 --> 00:46:50,600
The day after tomorrow,

721
00:46:51,480 --> 00:46:52,960
I'll go to Araya Group.

722
00:46:58,040 --> 00:46:58,720
Alright.

723
00:46:59,120 --> 00:47:01,120
Those in favor of purchasing the land development plan

724
00:47:01,160 --> 00:47:03,640
for a resort in northern Phuket,

725
00:47:04,040 --> 00:47:05,200
please raise your hands.

726
00:47:16,960 --> 00:47:17,960
Then it's settled.

727
00:47:18,240 --> 00:47:19,040
We'll purchase the land in Phuket

728
00:47:19,040 --> 00:47:20,440
after the New Year.

729
00:47:20,800 --> 00:47:22,400
Meeting adjourned for today.

730
00:47:27,280 --> 00:47:28,160
Secretary Piang,

731
00:47:28,840 --> 00:47:30,200
please get in touch with Mr. Yang

732
00:47:30,360 --> 00:47:31,880
about the land purchase in Phuket.

733
00:47:32,520 --> 00:47:34,040
Please keep it strictly professional.

734
00:47:34,880 --> 00:47:35,880
Understood.

735
00:47:51,360 --> 00:47:52,160
Ing...

736
00:47:54,400 --> 00:47:55,840
Grandpa has been trying to call you,

737
00:47:55,840 --> 00:47:56,920
but he hasn't been able to get through.

738
00:47:57,960 --> 00:47:59,920
He wants you to visit him for the New Year.

739
00:48:03,480 --> 00:48:05,080
Mm, I know.

740
00:48:07,680 --> 00:48:08,480
Ing,

741
00:48:09,400 --> 00:48:10,560
about the lawsuit,

742
00:48:12,000 --> 00:48:13,480
I want to ask you

743
00:48:13,520 --> 00:48:14,720
to think it over one more time.

744
00:48:16,240 --> 00:48:18,920
After all, Itt is still your brother.

745
00:48:20,840 --> 00:48:21,640
Is that so?

746
00:48:22,280 --> 00:48:24,080
When he was stabbing me in the back,

747
00:48:24,440 --> 00:48:25,960
did he see me as a brother?

748
00:48:27,800 --> 00:48:29,680
But he realizes he was wrong.

749
00:48:32,200 --> 00:48:33,520
And he's promised me

750
00:48:33,560 --> 00:48:34,360
that he'll stop.

751
00:48:38,960 --> 00:48:40,440
Tomorrow is New Year's Eve.

752
00:48:40,520 --> 00:48:42,280
I want you to come home for dinner,

753
00:48:43,040 --> 00:48:44,840
and I'll make him apologize to you.

754
00:48:46,320 --> 00:48:47,640
And if you're still mad,

755
00:48:48,600 --> 00:48:50,240
I'll even give him a beating for you.

756
00:48:50,280 --> 00:48:51,080
Is that fair?

757
00:48:54,240 --> 00:48:55,040
Oh, yeah?

758
00:49:04,120 --> 00:49:06,200
We're here to gather more information

759
00:49:06,640 --> 00:49:08,720
regarding Mr. Pruttha's case.

760
00:49:09,320 --> 00:49:10,680
Could you tell us

761
00:49:10,840 --> 00:49:13,640
what role Mr. Pongpruet had in the Pattaya project

762
00:49:14,160 --> 00:49:17,080
while you were working on it?

763
00:49:17,560 --> 00:49:20,480
Oh, he introduced me to the officials

764
00:49:20,520 --> 00:49:22,600
at various government agencies in Pattaya.

765
00:49:22,880 --> 00:49:23,880
During that time,

766
00:49:24,040 --> 00:49:26,840
did you have any shared financial interests?

767
00:49:28,960 --> 00:49:30,520
Financial interests?

768
00:49:35,000 --> 00:49:36,400
I was actually...

769
00:49:38,720 --> 00:49:40,360
hoping there would be some.

770
00:49:58,000 --> 00:49:59,360
When you decided to back out,

771
00:49:59,400 --> 00:50:00,760
why didn't you tell me right away?

772
00:50:00,760 --> 00:50:02,400
You ungrateful son.

773
00:50:02,600 --> 00:50:04,520
What are you doing? Can't you hear me?

774
00:50:05,000 --> 00:50:06,000
You should stop, Itt.

775
00:50:06,320 --> 00:50:07,760
Don't make things any worse.

776
00:50:07,920 --> 00:50:09,320
This is a very big deal.

777
00:50:09,320 --> 00:50:10,400
You really had no idea?

778
00:50:10,600 --> 00:50:12,920
The view from inside the room is different

779
00:50:13,280 --> 00:50:14,320
from the one up on the rooftop.

780
00:50:14,600 --> 00:50:15,800
Give Ing some time.

781
00:50:16,000 --> 00:50:17,880
No one gives a damn about me.

782
00:50:18,120 --> 00:50:19,720
They only care about what they can gain from me.

783
00:50:21,000 --> 00:50:22,280
I said, let go.

784
00:50:22,800 --> 00:50:24,360
What makes you think

785
00:50:24,880 --> 00:50:26,120
I'd ever submit to you?

786
00:50:26,200 --> 00:50:27,080
You idiot.
